    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"How many languages are there?\"\nsubtitle: \"Lin 211 • Section 1, Part 4\"\ndescription: \"[How many? (pdf)](https://uk.instructure.com/files/119829257/download?download_frd=1)\"\ndate: 09/02/2026\ncategories: [Getting Started]\nauthors:\n  - name: Kevin B McGowan\n    orcid: 0000-0002-8214-1901\n    email: kbmcgowan@uky.edu\ntbl-cap-location: bottom\nformat:\n  revealjs:\n    slide-number: c/t\n    width: 1600\n    height: 900\n    footer: \"Getting Started\"\n    incremental: false\n    scrollable: true\n    theme: [sky, includes/styles.scss]\n    template-partials:\n      - includes/title-slide.html\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n## What makes humans so special?\n\n:::: {.columns}\n\n::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n![An Australian Shepherd dog](images/Australian_Shepherd_1000.png)\n\n:::\n\n::: {.column width=\"60%\".incremental}\n\n- **linguistics** is the scientific study of language\n- **language** is the human capacity to symbolically represent thoughts, ideas, and feelings\n- and to experience those symbolic representations as meaning\n- human **languages** are structured systems for making articulated thoughts fully explicit\n- and critically depend on knowing (more or less) what the people around us know or believe, how they're feeling, and what they might be interested in\n- Even the brightest dog can’t do that\\!\n\n:::\n\n::::\n\n## Ling Link\n\n* Please go to [ethnologue.com](https://ethnologue.com/), Click on \"Languages\" on the left, click on any one of the huge list of languages that come up, and spend ~3 minutes answering the following questions with your neighbor:\n  * Examine the map. Where is this language spoken?\n  * Examine the information about population. How many people speak it? Is this a large number or a small number (read the info under \"Details\")?\n  * Examine the category of **language vitality**. Is this language at a risk of dying \\(read the info under \"Details\"\\)? Is it Stable?  Is it Institutional?\n  * What language family does the language belong to? Had you heard of that family before?\n\n## Take a guess\n\n::: {.r-fit-text style=\"margin-top: 200px;\" .incremental}\n\n- If you had to guess, how many different ways do you think there are on Earth to say 'Earth'? or 'love' or 'person'?\n- In other words, how many languages do you think there are on Earth?\n\n:::\n\n## Attendance Question\n\n- the attendance question is now unlocked on canvas\n- it is called: **attendance question (lecture day 4)**\n- the access code is: TARDIS\n\n## About 7,170 Languages\n\n- There are roughly 8.3 billion people: [8,319,554,735](https://worldpopulationclock.net/) on September 1st 2026\n- That could mean there are roughly 1,160,328 speakers per language, right?\n$$\n\\frac{8,319,554,735}{7,170} = 1,160,328\n$$\n\n## Top 20 Languages by First Language speakers\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](index_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-2-1.png){width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Most Spoken Languages on Earth\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_zf0ha6k7jtfe0lgzp86x = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_zf0ha6k7jtfe0lgzp86x\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '-1', j: 3 }, { i: '-1', j: 4 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_wo5swrvsqe00qc8g5m4k',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '-1', j: 2 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_1qnl949xk45x85rlvkgq',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '20', j: 1 }, { i: '20', j: 2 }, { i: '20', j: 3 }, { i: '20', j: 4 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_mr42y5o6o1qtprsfmy9k',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 }, { i: '0', j: 2 }, { i: '0', j: 3 